=============================================================================
rommsync-nx @VERSION@
=============================================================================

On-device RomM sync for a modded Nintendo Switch: a background sysmodule
(sys-rommsync) that syncs your saves and runs the download queue, plus an
Ultrahand / Tesla overlay (ovl-rommsync) to drive it.

  https://github.com/armaatus/rommsync-nx

This is a PRE-RELEASE that has not yet been run on a real console. Try it
on a spare SD card or an emuMMC with a NAND backup, against a RomM you do
not mind losing saves on.


YOU NEED
--------

  - A console running Atmosphere (the versions this build targets are
    under "Before you start" in docs/INSTALL.md)
  - Ultrahand (or Tesla), with the overlay menu working
  - ovl-sysmodules, to turn the sysmodule on and off
  - A RomM 5.4.0 or later server the console can reach, and an account
    on it you can sign into from a phone or a computer


INSTALL
-------

Unzip this archive onto the ROOT of your SD card, keeping the folder
structure. It merges with what is already there, adding six files and
one empty folder, and changing nothing else:

  atmosphere/contents/@TITLE_ID@/exefs.nsp    the sysmodule
  atmosphere/contents/@TITLE_ID@/toolbox.json what ovl-sysmodules lists it by
  atmosphere/contents/@TITLE_ID@/flags/       empty: the sysmodule is off
  switch/.overlays/ovl-rommsync.ovl                 the overlay
  config/rommsync/config.ini.example                a starting configuration
  README.txt                                        this file
  LICENSE

Note the last two: they land at the ROOT of the card under those names, so an
unrelated README.txt or LICENSE already sitting there is replaced.

Then, in order:

  1. The sysmodule ships DISABLED. There is no flags/boot2.flag in this
     archive, so nothing runs until you enable it -- use ovl-sysmodules,
     which is also how you stop it again. It creates that flag in the
     empty flags/ folder this archive ships; do not make it by hand.
  2. Copy config/rommsync/config.ini.example to config/rommsync/config.ini
     and set [server] url to your RomM.
  3. Open ovl-rommsync from the Ultrahand overlay menu, press Y for
     Settings, choose Pairing and press Pair. Open the address it shows in
     a browser signed in to RomM and enter the eight-character code; no
     password is ever typed on the console.


USING IT
--------

Saves sync on boot, every 30 minutes, and when you press Sync now
(Settings > Sync, then A). Nothing syncs while a game is running: a sync
that falls due waits until you close the game.

The server is the source of truth. Every save the console overwrites or
removes is copied to config/rommsync/.backup/ first. When a save changed
on both sides, Settings > Conflicts lets you keep the server's copy or put
this console's back and upload it (Keep local).

A save you delete in RomM is removed from the card too, after its backup.
Set on_server_delete = keep in config.ini to stop that.

Something not syncing? Settings > Log shows what the sysmodule last said.


UPGRADING
---------

Unzip a newer release over the top. The only files replaced are the six
listed above. config.ini, token.dat, device.dat, state.db, queue.json,
conflicts.db, rommsync.log and the .backup/ folder are not in the archive,
so your settings, your pairing, your sync state, your save backups and
your log survive.

From v1.0.0-rc1: saves now sync in RomM's shared "autosave" slot. The
first sync offers each save there: a newer copy already in RomM comes
down (yours backed up first), and a newer copy on the card shows up under
Conflicts. See "Upgrading" in docs/INSTALL.md.


THE FULL GUIDE
--------------

Start here; this page exists for every release:

  https://github.com/armaatus/rommsync-nx#readme

Install and pairing, step by step, and the configuration reference:

  https://github.com/armaatus/rommsync-nx/blob/main/docs/INSTALL.md
  https://github.com/armaatus/rommsync-nx/blob/main/docs/CONFIG.md

When a sync does not happen. sys-rommsync writes what went wrong to
config/rommsync/rommsync.log on this card; this page is what every line in
it means, and what to do about it:

  https://github.com/armaatus/rommsync-nx/blob/main/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md


